G1024.b:
⟪βραχύς⟫, -εῖα, -ύ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨מְעַט⁩ ;] ⟪short⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of time; ⟪short, little⟫: βραχύ, ⟦Acts 5:34|Ac 5:34⟧; μετὰ β., ⟦Luke 22:58|Lk 22:58⟧; β. τι, ⟪a short time⟫, ⟦Hebrews 2:7|He 2:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:9|9⟧ RV, mg.;
⟪(b)⟫ of distance: ⟦Acts 27:28|Ac 27:28⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of quantity or value, ⟪little, few⟫: ⟦John 6:7|Jo 6:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:7|He 2:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:9|9⟧ RV, txt.; pl., διὰ βραχέων, in few words, ⟦Hebrews 13:22|He 13:22⟧.†

G1053.b:
⟪Γαλατία⟫, -ας, ἡ, ⟪Galatia⟫;
⟪1.⟫ a gentilic region in Asia Minor, settled by Gauls (iii/B.C).
⟪2.⟫ A Roman Province which included this region (DB, ii, 85ff.): ⟦1 Corinthians 16:1|I Co 16:1⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:2|Ga 1:2⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:10|II Ti 4:10⟧ (T, Tr., mg., Γαλλίαν), ⟦1 Peter 1:1|I Pe 1:1⟧.†

G1065.b:
⟪γε⟫, enclitic postpositive particle, rarer in κοινή than in cl., giving special prominence to the word to which it is attached, distinguishing it as the least or the most important (Thayer, s.v.), ⟪indeed, at least, even⟫ (but not always translatable into English);
⟪1.⟫ used alone: ⟦Luke 11:8|Lk 11:8⟧ ⟦Luke 18:5|18:5⟧ ⟦Romans 8:32|Ro 8:32⟧.
⟪2.⟫ More freq. with other particles: αλλά γε, ⟦Luke 24:21|Lk 24:21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:2|I Co 9:2⟧; ἄρα γε, ⟦Matthew 7:20|Mt 7:20⟧ ⟦Matthew 17:26|17:26⟧, ⟦Acts 17:27|Ac 17:27⟧; ἆρά γε, ⟦Acts 8:30|Ac 8:30⟧; εἴ γε (Rec. εἴγε), ⟦2 Corinthians 5:3|II Co 5:3⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:4|Ga 3:4⟧, ⟦Ephesians 3:2|Eph 3:2⟧ ⟦Ephesians 4:21|4:21⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:23|Col 1:23⟧ (v. Meyer, Ellic., on Ga, Eph, ll. c.; Lft., on Ga, Col, ll. c.); εἰ δὲ μήγε, following an affirmation, ⟦Matthew 6:1|Mt 6:1⟧, ⟦Luke 10:6|Lk 10:6⟧ ⟦Luke 13:9|13:9⟧; a negation, ⟦Matthew 9:17|Mt 9:17⟧, ⟦Luke 5:36|Lk 5:36⟧, ⟦Luke 5:37|37⟧ ⟦Luke 14:32|14:32⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:16|II Co 11:16⟧; καί γε (Rec. καίγε, cl. καὶ . . . γε), ⟦Luke 19:42|Lk 19:42⟧ (WH om.), ⟦Acts 2:18|Ac 2:18⟧ ⟦Acts 17:27|17:27⟧; καίτοιγε (L καίτοι γε, Tr. καί τοι γε), ⟦John 4:2|Jo 4:2⟧; μενοῦνγε (v. s.v.); μήτι γε, v.s. μήτι; ὄφελόν, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:8|I Co 4:8⟧.†

G1074.b:
⟪γενεά⟫, -ᾶς, ἡ
(< γίγνομαι), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨דּוֹר⁩, ⁨דֹּר⁩ (Cremer, 148) ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪race, stock, family⟫ (in NT, γέννημα, q.v.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪generation⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of the contemporary members of a family: pl., ⟦Matthew 1:17|Mt 1:17⟧ (cf. ⟦Genesis 31:3|Ge 31:3⟧, ⁨מוֹלֶדֶת⁩); metaph., of those alike in character, in bad sense, ⟦Matthew 17:17|Mt 17:17⟧, ⟦Mark 9:19|Mk 9:19⟧, ⟦Luke 9:41|Lk 9:41⟧ ⟦Luke 16:8|16:8⟧, ⟦Acts 2:40|Ac 2:40⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of all the people of a given period: ⟦Matthew 24:34|Mt 24:34⟧, ⟦Mark 13:30|Mk 13:30⟧, ⟦Luke 21:32|Lk 21:32⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:15|Phl 2:15⟧; pl., ⟦Luke 1:48|Lk 1:48⟧; esp. of the Jewish people, ⟦Matthew 11:16|Mt 11:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:39|12:39⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:41|41⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:42|42⟧, ⟦Matthew 12:45|45⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:4|16:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:36|23:36⟧, ⟦Mark 8:12|Mk 8:12⟧, ⟦Mark 8:38|38⟧ ⟦Luke 7:31|Lk 7:31⟧ ⟦Luke 11:29|11:29⟧, ⟦Luke 11:30|30-32⟧, ⟦Luke 11:50|50⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|51⟧ ⟦Luke 17:25|17:25⟧, ⟦Acts 13:36|Ac 13:36⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:10|He 3:10⟧ (LXX); τὴν γ. αὐτοῦ τίς διηγήσεται, ⟦Acts 8:33|Ac 8:33⟧ (LXX);
	⟪(c)⟫ the period covered by the life-time of a generation, used loosely in pl. of successive ages: ⟦Acts 14:16|Ac 14:16⟧ ⟦Acts 15:21|15:21⟧, ⟦Ephesians 3:5|Eph 3:5⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:26|Col 1:26⟧; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ. (= ⁨לִדוֹר וָדוֹר⁩, al.), ⟦Luke 34:17|Lk 34:17⟧, al), ⟦Luke 1:50|Lk 1:50⟧; εἰς πάσας τὰς γ. τοῦ αἰῶνος τῶν αἰώνων, ⟦Ephesians 3:21|Eph 3:21⟧ (Ellic, in l.; DCG, i, 639f.). †

G1076.b:
* ⟪γενεαλογία⟫, -ας, ἡ (v. previous word);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪the making of a pedigree⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪a genealogy⟫: pl., ⟦1 Timothy 1:4|I Ti 1:4⟧, ⟦Titus 3:9|Tit 3:9⟧ (v. CGT, in l., and ib. Intr., xlix ff.; DB, ii, p. 141).†

G1077.b:
* ⟪γενέσια⟫, -ων, τά, neut. pl. of adj. -ιος, -ον, relating to birth (< γένεσις);
⟪1.⟫ in Attic Gk., ⟪a commemoration of the dead⟫.
⟪2.⟫ In late Gk., ⟪a birthday feast⟫ (= cl. γενέθλια; so in π., v. MM, Exp., x; cf. also Rutherford, NPhr., 184): ⟦Matthew 14:6|Mt 14:6⟧, ⟦Mark 6:21|Mk 6:21⟧.†

G1093.b:
⟪γῆ⟫, γῆς, ἡ,
[in LXX for ⁨אֶרֶץ⁩, ⁨אֲדָמָה⁩, etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪the earth⟫, ⟪world⟫: ⟦Luke 21:35|Lk 21:35⟧, ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:13|He 11:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:10|Re 3:10⟧, al.; opp. to οὐρανός, ⟦Matthew 5:18|Mt 5:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 11:25|11:25⟧, ⟦Mark 13:27|Mk 13:27⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪land⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ opp. to sea or water: ⟦Mark 4:1|Mk 4:1⟧, ⟦Luke 5:3|Lk 5:3⟧, ⟦John 6:21|Jo 6:21⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ as subject to cultivation: ⟦Matthew 13:5|Mt 13:5⟧, ⟦Mark 4:8|Mk 4:8⟧, ⟦Luke 13:7|Lk 13:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:7|He 6:7⟧, al.;
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪the ground⟫: ⟦Matthew 10:29|Mt 10:29⟧, ⟦Mark 8:6|Mk 8:6⟧, ⟦Luke 24:5|Lk 24:5⟧, ⟦John 8:6|Jo 8:6⟧, al.;
	⟪(d)⟫ ⟪a region⟫, ⟪country⟫: ⟦Luke 4:25|Lk 4:25⟧, ⟦Romans 9:28|Ro 9:28⟧, ⟦James 5:17|Ja 5:17⟧; γῆ Ἰσραήλ, ⟦Matthew 2:20|Mt 2:20⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:21|21⟧; Χαλδαίων, ⟦Acts 7:4|Ac 7:4⟧; ἡ Ἰουδαία γῆ, ⟦John 3:22|Jo 3:22⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟦Acts 7:3|Ac 7:3⟧.
